  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 items closed (6 at start, 1 arrived while working). Three results arrived during the work and changed decisions; the corrections are recorded.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price\n- Metformin: 3 messages (patient, pharmacy, pharmacy follow-up) treated as one request. Renewed 1000 mg BID, 90 days, 1 refill (mr-t0002). The corrected eGFR of 58 still allows it, and the outside HbA1c of 7.1% (collected 08/19/2026) is within 6 months.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: renewed at first (mr-t0001). Then the lab corrected the 10/06 creatinine to 1.49. That is 35% above the 1.10 baseline from before the 09/18 dose increase, so the protocol treats it as a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled mr-t0001; nothing had been dispensed. No new ACE order was placed, and the old order mr-00295 stays stopped. Created urgent PCP review task-t0011.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: renewed at first (mr-t0003), because the 08/27 outside potassium of 5.9 was hemolyzed and the last valid one was 4.5. I also ordered a BMP (sr-t0006). Then a valid outside BMP from 10/20 arrived with potassium 5.8. I cancelled mr-t0003, placed no new order, and created urgent PCP review task-t0012. The old order mr-00283 stays stopped, and BMP sr-t0006 is still open.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb\n- Metformin 500 mg BID: renewed, 90 days, 1 refill (mr-t0005). The eGFR of 39 from 10/14 was entered in error (wrong patient's specimen); the valid eGFR is 92/90 and HbA1c is 6.9%.\n- Lisinopril: at first a 30-day, 0-refill supply (mr-t0004) plus a BMP order (sr-t0007), because there was no BMP in the last 12 months. A BMP from 10/22 then arrived with potassium 4.6, so I replaced it with a 90-day, 1-refill order (mr-t0010). BMP sr-t0007 is no longer needed, but I had no tool to cancel it, so please cancel it.\n\n- Each patient got a portal reply, and each has a telephone note (doc-t0016/17/18) explaining the decisions and corrections.\n- The three new results (inbox-a0001, a0003, a0004) are still open in your results queue for you to see. I did not touch the other items in your results queue (other patients, outside this protocol).",
